  +"perf(mad-iqa, hdrvdp): run the Bluestein batches on the serial path too"
  +"perf(mad-iqa): fuse the csf/gabor filter multiply into the inverse fft"
parity:
  score_hi/score_lo identical across all three stack levels (batch and
  fusion are bit-exact). mad-iqa tests incl. plane_goldens pass serial
  and --features parallel on the tip. The cpu-profile harness could not
  be rebuilt (zenmetrics-api fails against the mid-migration fast-ssim2
  sibling checkout, unrelated), so the photo 18.613801284574702 sentinel
  was not re-run on this stack.
notes:
  3355x2516 serial baseline row measured on the stack parent (upstream tip,
  mad-iqa untouched). i265 post-sweep doc records mad 1t 26.9s — that leg ran
  the metrics-parallel binary pinned to one core, i.e. the same batch8 code
  these rows enable for the default build.
  run-heavy/niced environment; absolute ms are ±5% run to run.
